{"nodes": [{"id": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "label": "CrySLDoc Correctness Audit", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_five_round_audit_method", "label": "Five-Round Audit Method", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Static reading of every file plus empirical verification (reflection harnesses on private pipeline methods, custom .crysl rules, side-by-side git HEAD vs working-tree builds, whole-site link checking, full end-to-end JDK 21 runs). The most useful result of round 5 is negative: after four rounds each uncovering output-corrupting defects, a sweep that finds none is treated as the first real evidence the deterministic pipeline has stabilised."}, {"id": "audit_c1_undocumented_environment_variables", "label": "C1 \u2014 Eleven Undocumented Environment Variables", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CRYSLDOC_COMPILE_CHECK=0 disables the compile gate the whole secure-example design rests on, and nothing told an operator it existed. Five of the variables were introduced by the audit work itself; adding a tunable without documenting it is how the gap formed. Fixed by documenting all thirteen in README.md rather than removing the tunables."}, {"id": "audit_c2_positional_list_pairing", "label": "C2 \u2014 Positional List Coupling in Two More Loops", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Correct today only by accidents of ordering, not enforced invariants. Fixed by resolving ComposedRule through a Map<String, ComposedRule> keyed by class name so the positional invariant is removed rather than merely documented."}, {"id": "audit_c3_populatepredicatetree_control_flow", "label": "C3 \u2014 populatePredicateTree Unguarded Lookup and return-vs-continue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unreachable code that would be wrong if reached is still worth correcting, because the reasoning that makes it safe is not local to the method."}, {"id": "audit_c4_llmexplanation_uninitialised", "label": "C4 \u2014 ComposedRule.llmExplanation Never Initialised", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_b1_traceback_leaked_into_pages", "label": "B1 \u2014 Python Tracebacks and Build Paths Published as Code Examples", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documentation intended for readers leaked the build machine's filesystem layout, and the place a code example belongs was filled with a stack trace. Fixed with Utils.summarizeGenerationFailure producing one publication-safe line while the unabridged text moves to a Full diagnostics section of the failure report, so nothing is lost."}, {"id": "audit_b2_trustanchor_rewrite_corrupts_code", "label": "B2 \u2014 TrustAnchor Known-Mistake Rewrite Corrupts Correct Code", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The regex damaged valid TrustAnchor(X509Certificate, byte[]) calls (dropping nameConstraints, a PKIX security control) and still did not repair the case it targeted. Removed rather than narrowed, because the compile-and-repair loop already handles hallucinated overloads without the risk of silently editing correct code."}, {"id": "audit_b3_unconditional_crysl_contract_dump", "label": "B3 \u2014 Unconditional CrySL Contract Debug Dump", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_b4_keyagreement_orphan_label", "label": "B4 \u2014 KeyAgreement.crysl Aggregates the Wrong Event Label", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Found by scanning all 51 rules for labels defined but never referenced \u2014 gs2 was the only orphan in the entire rule set, which is the signature of exactly this kind of typo. Flagged as a local edit to an upstream-synced rule that must be reported to CROSSINGTUD/Crypto-API-Rules or it returns on the next sync."}, {"id": "audit_b5_dead_ftltemplateloaderfromjar", "label": "B5 \u2014 Dead FTLTemplateLoaderFromJar with getResource().getPath() Defect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_a1_wrong_state_machine_diagram", "label": "A1 \u2014 49 of 51 Pages Show Another Class's State-Machine Diagram", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "createSidebar sorted the caller's composedRuleList in place while cryslRuleList stayed unsorted, and createSinglePage paired the two by index. Fixed at both levels \u2014 sidebar sorts a copy and single-page lookup goes through a Map<String, CrySLRule> \u2014 because either change alone fixes today's symptom but only both remove the class of bug."}, {"id": "audit_a2_no_rule_level_failure_isolation", "label": "A2 \u2014 No Rule-Level Failure Isolation in the Composition Loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A skipped rule is removed from both lists so the two stay aligned and no partial page is written; a summary naming every skipped rule and its cause is printed after composition."}, {"id": "audit_a3_explanation_cache_placeholder_reuse", "label": "A3 \u2014 Explanation Cache Cannot Distinguish Answer from Placeholder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first fix was incomplete \u2014 it corrected the outer reuse decision but LLMService still short-circuited on file existence, so a placeholder was rewritten with itself. The detector was moved into Utils so both layers share one definition and 'skip the call' cannot disagree with 'reuse the file'."}, {"id": "audit_a4_compile_gate_classpath", "label": "A4 \u2014 Compile Gate Validated Against the Generator's Own Classpath", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Examples were validated against Xtext/Soot/Guava/FreeMarker, libraries a documentation reader will not have, so the gate could not mean what it claimed. Fixed to a JDK-only classpath with two escape hatches instead of a hard-coded exception. Cost: the Cookie rule now fails without CRYSLDOC_COMPILE_CLASSPATH \u2014 a real regression that predicting did not prevent."}, {"id": "audit_a5_import_time_directory_side_effect", "label": "A5 \u2014 Importing llm_utils Creates a Directory as a Side Effect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Directory creation belongs in the functions that write files, not at import time where --help, a syntax check or an editor's autocomplete triggers it."}, {"id": "audit_a6_parameter_name_label_corruption", "label": "A6 \u2014 Parameter Names String-Replaced into Graphviz Labels", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Global String.replace of each parameter name with its type corrupted labels whenever a name occurred elsewhere (p and g occur inside both the method name and 'BigInteger'). Fixed by building the label directly from structured parameters so no replacement happens and no corruption is possible."}, {"id": "audit_a7_generic_type_truncation", "label": "A7 \u2014 Generic Parameter Types Truncated at the Last Dot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_n1_stringencryption_violates_bundled_rules", "label": "N1 \u2014 StringEncryption Crashes and Violates Four of the Project's Own Rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For a tool whose purpose is generating secure-usage documentation, shipping a compiled example its own bundled rules would reject is a credibility problem independent of the crash. Rewritten to comply rather than deleted, because git history shows it was added deliberately as a user-study code example."}, {"id": "audit_n2_llm_payload_cache_staleness", "label": "N2 \u2014 LLM Input Payload Cache Is Existence-Gated", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both payload and sanitized derivative are now written unconditionally: these are local operations, negligible beside the API call that follows, and unconditional writes remove the failure mode entirely rather than papering over it with a hash check."}, {"id": "audit_n3_system_exit_in_library_code", "label": "N3 \u2014 System.exit(255) Inside Library Code", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_n4_dead_utils_methods", "label": "N4 \u2014 Four Dead Public Utils Methods, One Latently Unsafe", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unreachable code that would need real work to be correct is removed rather than speculatively repaired \u2014 the same disposition applied to the dead Constant.java."}, {"id": "audit_n5_javadoc_link_misdirection", "label": "N5 \u2014 Cookie JavaDoc Link Silently Redirects to an Unrelated Page", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The URL is now computed once in ClassEventForb.getJavaDocUrl and carried on ComposedRule.javaDocUrl, replacing a base URL hard-coded in two places; JDK classes keep Java 8 URLs to avoid the module-qualified paths modern JavaSE JavaDoc requires."}, {"id": "audit_n6_template_markup_defects", "label": "N6 \u2014 Markup Defects in frontpage.ftl and sidebar.ftl", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "audit_n7_substring_variable_matching", "label": "N7 \u2014 Substring-Based Variable-to-Method Matching Yields Position -1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selection with contains() disagreed with the indexOf-based position computation that followed it; a shared FunctionUtils.hasParameterNamed parses the parameter list and compares exactly so selection and position agree."}, {"id": "audit_n8_api_retry_and_timeout_defaults", "label": "N8 \u2014 API Robustness Rested on the SDK's Default Two Retries", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Centralising max_retries/timeout in llm_env.client_kwargs() rather than repeating literals at eight construction sites also avoids widening the duplication the audit already flags."}, {"id": "audit_golden_output_regression_diffing", "label": "Golden-Output Byte-Diff Regression Control", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capturing all 51 pages and byte-diffing after a change proves blast radius and confirms latent fixes produce zero output change. It answers 'did this change break anything' but cannot catch defects that predate the baseline \u2014 A1, A6 and A7 were wrong before any baseline existed, so every baseline enshrined them. Both kinds of check are needed; the technique lives in /tmp, not in the repo."}, {"id": "audit_verification_gaps", "label": "Honest Verification Gaps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Fixed' and 'proven fixed' are different claims. The LLM path has never run against live API traffic; ten fixes are compile- and read-verified only because no bundled rule exercises their trigger shape; N2 is proven by code inspection, not by an end-to-end run."}, {"id": "audit_python_llm_layer_duplication", "label": "Python LLM Layer Duplication", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four copy-pasted client constructions, two copies of make_rag_context, and llm_code_writer_secure.py reimplementing ~10 llm_utils.py helpers that have already drifted. Two same-named helpers with different signatures in one codebase made a wrong diagnosis look well-supported during round 3, and duplication is why several fixes needed the same edit in multiple places."}], "edges": [{"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_c1_undocumented_environment_variables", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_c2_positional_list_pairing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_c3_populatepredicatetree_control_flow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_c4_llmexplanation_uninitialised", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_b1_traceback_leaked_into_pages", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_b2_trustanchor_rewrite_corrupts_code", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_b3_unconditional_crysl_contract_dump", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_b4_keyagreement_orphan_label", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_b5_dead_ftltemplateloaderfromjar", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a1_wrong_state_machine_diagram", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a2_no_rule_level_failure_isolation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a3_explanation_cache_placeholder_reuse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a4_compile_gate_classpath", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a5_import_time_directory_side_effect", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a6_parameter_name_label_corruption", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_a7_generic_type_truncation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n1_stringencryption_violates_bundled_rules", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n2_llm_payload_cache_staleness", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n3_system_exit_in_library_code", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n4_dead_utils_methods", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n5_javadoc_link_misdirection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n6_template_markup_defects", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "AUDIT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "audit_crysldoc_correctness_audit", "target": "audit_n7_substring_variable_matching", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "s